add('b166','整合明挖隧道的地表界面、支撐、水壓與回填階段~Integrate surface interfaces, bracing, water pressure and backfilling in cut-and-cover tunnels','開挖、結構施工與回填具有不同荷載路徑，竣工模型不能取代施工模型。~Excavation, structural work and backfilling have different load paths; the final model does not replace staged models.','長 100 m、深 8 m，寬由 14 增為 16 m，土方由 11200 增為 12800 m3，增加 14.3%；支撐跨距及水力影響不只按體積同比放大。~At 100 m length and 8 m depth, widening from 14 to 16 m raises excavation from 11200 to 12800 m3, by 14.3%; brace spans and hydraulic effects do not merely scale with volume.',r'''
開挖尺度與地表影響~Excavation scale and surface impact§明挖把地下結構施工直接連到地表交通、管線和鄰房，開挖寬度也改變支撐跨距與土體卸載。土方體積只是物流量級，不能代表所有變形風險；工法選擇應把永久箱體、臨時圍護和地表使用需求放在同一斷面。~Cut-and-cover directly couples underground construction to traffic, utilities and neighbours. Width changes brace spans and unloading as well as spoil volume. Volume describes logistics rather than all deformation risks; compare the permanent box, temporary retention and surface-use demands in one section.§V=L*B*H=100 m*14 m*8 m=11200 m3§比對探測管線、道路分期及開挖邊界的共同座標~Compare detected utilities, road stages and excavation limits in shared coordinates§只按土方安排忽略管線支承，既有設施因卸載或位移受損~A spoil-only plan misses utility support and damages services through unloading or movement§土方體積相同就代表兩個明挖工程風險相同~Equal excavation volume means identical risk for two cut-and-cover projects
側向土壓與變形條件~Lateral soil pressure and movement conditions§主動土壓需要足夠牆體位移才可動員，鄰房敏感區的剛性支撐未必允許達到這個狀態。地表超載與水壓應分開處理，不能將總壓力都乘同一係數；簡化三角分布只用來理解量級，支撐牆需考慮分階段受力。~Active pressure requires sufficient wall movement, which stiff restraint near sensitive buildings may prevent. Treat surcharge and water separately rather than multiplying total pressure by one coefficient. A triangular diagram gives scale, while a supported wall needs staged force redistribution and movement compatibility.§resultant=0.5*Ka*gamma*H^2=0.5*0.33*18 kN/m3*(8 m)^2=190.1 kN/m§將牆體測斜與土層、超載及水位狀態共同比對~Compare wall inclinometers with strata, surcharge and groundwater conditions§用主動壓力描述幾乎不動的牆，低估支撐反力~Active pressure applied to a nearly restrained wall understates brace reactions§所有擋土牆都可以直接使用完全主動土壓~Every retaining wall can directly use fully active earth pressure
支撐軸力與溫度~Brace force and temperature§鋼支撐除了承受地層作用，也會隨溫度伸縮，受到拘束時產生額外軸力。荷重增加可能是熱效應而非牆後土壓增加，零點時間因此重要；比較力值要同步看溫度、牆移和接頭滑移，避免用單支荷重計判斷地層。~Steel braces expand thermally and develop extra force when restrained. A force increase can reflect temperature rather than rising earth pressure, making zero time important. Compare force with temperature, wall movement and joint slip instead of diagnosing ground solely from one load cell.§fullRestraintForce=E*A*alpha*dT=200 GPa*0.01 m2*12e-6/K*10 K=240 kN§同步量測支撐溫度、軸力及兩端牆體位移~Measure brace temperature, axial force and both wall-end movements simultaneously§日照升溫造成力峰被誤判地層失穩，錯誤調整支撐~Solar heating creates a force peak mistaken for ground instability and prompts an incorrect brace change§支撐荷重變大就只能是土壓增加~Increasing brace force can only mean increasing earth pressure
底部隆起與抗浮區分~Base heave and uplift distinction§軟黏土底部隆起與承壓水造成的水力抬升有不同機制，不能以同一重量比處理。開挖卸載降低上覆應力，地層剪切與水壓都可能變得重要；調查需把不排水強度、滲透層和測壓水位分開建模。~Undrained clay heave and hydraulic uplift are different mechanisms and cannot share one simple weight ratio. Excavation removes overburden, increasing the importance of shear stability and pore pressure. Model undrained strength, permeable layers and piezometric level separately rather than merging all bottom movement.§waterUplift=gammaW*h*A=9.81 kN/m3*5 m*100 m2=4905 kN§比較底部位移、分層孔壓及地層強度資料~Compare base movement, interval pore pressures and ground-strength evidence§把水力抬升當普通沉陷調整標高，未處理真正水壓~Hydraulic uplift is treated as ordinary settlement correction without addressing the pressure source§基底往上動的所有原因都屬同一種失效~Every cause of upward base movement is the same failure mechanism
箱體自重與施工抗浮~Box weight and temporary flotation§永久覆土可提供重量，但施工中尚未回填時並不存在這份抗浮作用。空箱體、局部回填與封頂後各有不同邊界，水位也可能回升；重量帳必須只計入當階段確實存在且可傳力的部分，不得提前借用竣工狀態。~Permanent cover supplies weight but is absent before backfilling. Empty boxes, partial fill and completed roofs have different boundaries and may encounter rising groundwater. Count only weight physically present and connected in each stage rather than borrowing resistance from the completed structure.§weightToUplift=presentWeight/uplift=6000 kN/4905 kN=1.223, not a code factor§逐階段核對實際重量、回填範圍與可達水位~Audit actual weight, backfill extent and possible water levels at every stage§尚未回填便使用永久覆土重量，空箱體出現抬升~Using future cover weight allows an unbackfilled box to lift§竣工抗浮合格就能保證每個施工階段都抗浮~Passing permanent flotation checks guarantees every construction stage resists uplift
防水接縫與穿牆構件~Waterproof joints and penetrations§明挖箱體常有施工縫、伸縮縫及大量管線穿牆，止水連續性由這些界面控制。接縫位移與水壓可能同時存在，單獨材料試驗不能證明安裝系統；驗證需把預埋位置、固定狀態及兩側結構變形連在一起。~Cut-and-cover boxes contain construction joints, movement joints and penetrations that govern waterproof continuity. Movement and pressure can coexist, so isolated material tests do not prove installation. Link embedded position, restraint and deformation of adjacent structure rather than checking the seal alone.§jointStrain=movement/freeSealLength=4 mm/80 mm=0.05§核對止水帶連續、穿牆套管及接縫變形紀錄~Audit waterstop continuity, wall sleeves and joint-movement records§穿牆套管與止水細部不連續，漏水沿界面繞過膜材~A discontinuous sleeve detail lets water bypass the membrane along an interface§箱體牆面不裂就能保證所有穿牆位置都不漏~Uncracked box walls guarantee every penetration remains watertight
支撐拆換與荷載轉移~Brace removal and load transfer§臨時支撐拆除將側向荷載轉到永久樓板和牆，混凝土齡期與接頭完成度決定能否接手。竣工樓板存在不代表當天已具備預期剛度，開口也會切斷壓力路徑；拆換模型需按實際順序逐階段檢核。~Removing temporary braces transfers lateral actions to slabs and walls whose age and joint completion govern engagement. A slab's presence does not prove its intended stiffness, and openings interrupt compression paths. Assess removal in the actual sequence rather than using only the final configuration.§transferredReaction=removedBraceForce/engagedSlabWidth=900 kN/6 m=150 kN/m§對照樓板成熟證據、接頭完成及拆換前後應變~Compare slab maturity, joint completion and strains before and after load transfer§接頭尚未傳力就拆支撐，牆移突增並使樓板邊緣開裂~Removing a brace before joint engagement increases wall movement and cracks slab edges§永久樓板澆置完成就能立即取代全部臨時支撐~A freshly cast permanent slab immediately replaces every temporary brace
鄰房沉陷與角變形~Neighbour settlement and angular distortion§總沉陷與差異沉陷對建物的影響不同，剛體下沉可能不造成同樣裂縫，而局部角變形會擠壓門窗或拉開砌體。量測點需與建物結構分區相連，原有裂縫也應先記錄；不能把單一最大沉陷值當成全部損傷指標。兩測點沉陷差除跨距是平均沉陷坡度；要判別造成損傷的角變形，還須區分整體剛體傾斜與局部變形。~Total and differential settlements affect buildings differently: rigid movement can produce less cracking than local distortion. Connect survey points to structural divisions and document existing cracks. One maximum settlement value does not capture deformation patterns or establish damage causation by itself. Settlement difference divided by span is a mean settlement slope; damage-related angular distortion requires separating overall rigid-body tilt from local deformation.§meanSettlementSlope=settlementDifference/span=6 mm/12000 mm=0.0005 rad; rigid-body tilt has not been removed§將建物水準、傾斜與原有裂縫圖按結構跨間比較~Compare building levels, tilt and baseline cracks by structural bay§平均沉陷小但局部差異大，砌體開裂被單一數值漏判~Small mean settlement hides local differential movement that cracks masonry§平均沉陷很小就代表鄰房一定沒有損傷~Small average settlement guarantees no damage to neighbouring buildings
回填壓實與箱頂荷載~Backfill compaction and roof loading§回填不只增加永久覆土，也會帶來施工機具與壓實作用；不對稱堆置可使箱體受扭或側壓不均。填料剛度與排水影響後續沉陷，不能只看壓實度數字；施工階段的機具位置和覆土厚度需要一起核對。~Backfill adds construction plant and compaction effects as well as permanent overburden; asymmetric placement changes lateral loading. Fill stiffness and drainage govern later settlement, beyond one density result. Check plant position and cover depth together when assessing temporary roof demand.§overburdenPressure=unitWeight*depth=20 kN/m3*2 m=40 kPa§對照分層回填高程、機具位置及箱頂應變~Compare lift levels, equipment locations and roof strains§薄覆土上集中機具荷載讓箱頂局部超載，平均覆土帳未反映~Concentrated plant above thin cover overloads the roof despite acceptable average fill§回填越快完成就能保證施工階段更安全~Faster completion of backfilling guarantees safer construction stages
地表恢復與地下資產交接~Surface restoration and underground handover§道路恢復後，地下接縫、排水和檢查孔可能變得難以接近，維護動線須在交接時確認。竣工圖應記錄實際高程與管線改道，不能只保留原設計；地表平順也不能證明回填長期不沉陷，需建立後續比較基準。~After road restoration, joints, drains and access points become harder to reach, making maintenance access part of handover. Record as-built levels and utility diversions rather than design alone. A smooth surface does not establish long-term fill stability, so retain a postconstruction baseline.§Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.01,0.02,0.02 m; combinedStandardUncertainty=sqrt(0.01^2+0.02^2+0.02^2)=0.03 m for assumed independent components; not a measured survey-closure residual§核對竣工管線、檢查通道及道路沉陷基準點~Audit as-built utilities, inspection access and road-settlement reference points§維修口被道路設施遮住，使早期堵塞無法檢查清理~Road installations conceal maintenance openings and prevent early blockage inspection§道路恢復平整就表示全部地下工程已完成驗證~A smooth restored road proves all underground works have been verified
''')

add('b167','追蹤逆打樓板、預置柱與連續壁的分階段荷載~Track staged loads in top-down slabs, plunge columns and diaphragm walls','永久構件會先作臨時支撐，施工有效長度和接頭狀態不可沿用竣工值。~Permanent members first act as temporary support; construction lengths and joint states differ from final values.','樓板軸向面積 0.30 m2、模數 30 GPa 固定，跨長由 20 增為 25 m，理想軸向剛度由 450 降為 360 MN/m，降低 20%；開口與接頭另會減弱。~At area 0.30 m2 and modulus 30 GPa, increasing length from 20 to 25 m lowers ideal axial stiffness from 450 to 360 MN/m, by 20%; openings and joints add further reductions.',r'''
永久樓板的早期支撐~Permanent slabs as early braces§逆打先建立部分永久樓板，讓它們在向下開挖時支撐連續壁。樓板此時承受水平壓力與自身施工荷載，和竣工垂直受彎狀態不同；接頭、開口與混凝土齡期決定可用剛度，不能把全樓完成模型直接套用。~Top-down slabs brace diaphragm walls while excavation proceeds below them. They carry lateral compression and construction loads, unlike only their final vertical bending role. Joints, openings and concrete age define available stiffness, preventing direct use of a fully completed-building model.§axialStiffness=E*A/L=30 GPa*0.30 m2/20 m=450 MN/m§對照樓板齡期、接頭狀態及牆體位移與板內應變~Compare slab age and joints with wall movement and in-plane strain§未完成的板牆連接被當成剛接，牆移超過預估~An incomplete slab-wall connection is assumed rigid and wall movement exceeds prediction§永久樓板的施工受力必然與竣工受力完全相同~Permanent slabs have identical construction-stage and final-state loading
預置柱軸力與未支撐長度~Plunge-column force and unbraced length§預置柱在土體逐步挖除時暴露更長區段，樓板尚未完成處不能提供側向拘束。柱同時支承上方已建結構，軸力可能增加而有效長度也增加；檢查最不利施工階段比只看竣工樓層高度更重要。~Excavation exposes longer plunge-column lengths, and unfinished slabs provide no lateral restraint. Columns support completed upper work, so axial force and unbraced length can increase together. Identify the critical temporary stage rather than using only final storey heights.§EulerRatio=(oldLength/newLength)^2=(4 m/8 m)^2=0.25 at unchanged EI and end conditions§逐階段確認柱暴露長度、側向連接及累積軸力~Confirm exposed length, lateral connections and accumulated force at each stage§誤用竣工短柱長度高估施工屈曲能力，柱出現側彎~Final short-column length overstates temporary buckling resistance and the column bows§每層最後都有樓板所以施工柱永遠按一層高度算~Final slabs at every level make construction columns always one storey long
柱位偏差與荷載偏心~Column positioning and load eccentricity§預置柱深埋端的偏位難以在後續修正，柱頂和柱底不共線會讓垂直荷載產生彎矩。平面位置合格也不代表垂直度合格，需沿深度量測；局部接頭可能吸收幾何差，但不可因此忽略偏心力和施工容差。~Embedded plunge-column offsets are difficult to correct, and misaligned ends convert vertical force into bending. Correct plan position does not prove verticality; survey through depth. Connections may accommodate geometry, but eccentric force and construction tolerance still require explicit assessment.§M=N*e=3000 kN*0.025 m=75 kNm§比較柱頂、樓板交點及可取得深部軸線量測~Compare column tops, slab intersections and available deep-axis measurements§柱底偏位被地表控制點漏掉，上方荷載形成額外彎矩~A hidden base offset escapes surface control and adds moment under upper loads§柱頂位置正確就能保證整支預置柱完全垂直~Correct column-top position guarantees a perfectly vertical plunge column
樓板開口與壓力繞行~Slab openings and force detours§出土孔和機具孔切斷板內壓力路徑，荷載必須經邊梁或剩餘板帶繞行。以總板寬計算軸向剛度會高估支撐，洞角還可能出現應力集中；臨時封板時序也應列入模型，不能假設最終完整板提前存在。~Muck and plant openings interrupt in-plane compression, forcing it through edge beams or remaining strips. Gross slab width overstates restraint and corners concentrate stress. Include temporary closure timing rather than assuming the final continuous slab exists during excavation.§netArea=grossArea-openingLoss=0.60 m2-0.20 m2=0.40 m2§核對每階段開口範圍、洞邊鋼筋與板內應變分布~Check staged opening extents, edge reinforcement and in-plane strain distributions§出土孔臨時加大卻未更新模型，剩餘板帶壓裂~An enlarged access hole is omitted from the model and the remaining strip cracks§樓板只要厚度足夠就可以忽略出土孔位置~Adequate slab thickness permits muck-opening locations to be ignored
牆板接頭與剪力交接~Wall-slab joints and shear transfer§樓板與連續壁接頭需傳遞施工水平作用及永久荷載，預留筋、接合器和界面品質共同控制。回填或粉塵可能污染隱蔽接面，名義鋼筋量不能證明接頭已動員；需在下一階段開挖前確認完整的力線與品質證據。~Wall-slab joints transfer temporary lateral and permanent actions through bars, couplers and interface quality. Soil or dust can contaminate concealed surfaces, so nominal reinforcement does not prove engagement. Confirm the complete load path and quality evidence before relying on the joint in the next stage.§averageShear=V/A=900 kN/0.30 m2=3 MPa, before detailed joint checks§核對接合器、接面清理與接頭位移及裂縫紀錄~Check couplers, surface preparation and joint movement and cracking records§接頭局部空洞導致剪力集中，樓板整體強度合格仍滑移~Local joint voids concentrate shear and allow slip despite adequate slab strength§鋼筋數量符合就代表牆板接頭已完全驗證~Correct reinforcement count proves complete verification of the wall-slab joint
樓板下出土與荷載歷程~Under-slab excavation and loading history§樓板下開挖會移除原先土體支承，永久板和預置柱逐漸接手荷載。施工機具、土堆與運輸動線產生的暫時荷載可能比服務荷載更集中；材料帳和進度圖必須轉成荷載歷程，不能只描述挖了多少土。~Excavation below slabs removes soil support and transfers action to permanent slabs and plunge columns. Equipment, stockpiles and transport create concentrated temporary loads. Convert logistics and progress into a load history rather than describing only excavated volume or completed floor area.§stockpilePressure=unitWeight*height=18 kN/m3*2 m=36 kPa§對照土堆高度、機具位置和樓板下方已開挖範圍~Compare stockpile height and plant positions with the excavated footprint beneath slabs§同一樓板上堆土而下方支承已移除，局部彎曲增加~Stockpiling above an excavated unsupported area increases local slab bending§樓板設計承受使用荷載就能承受任何施工堆料~A slab designed for service loads can carry any construction stockpile
地下水卸載與地層回彈~Groundwater unloading and ground rebound§開挖減少總應力，降水又增加有效應力，兩者可能造成方向相反的變形。底部回彈與鄰地沉陷可以同時發生，不能用一個水位或沉陷點代表整個場域；模型需保留不同土層壓縮性和排水時間尺度。~Excavation reduces total stress while dewatering increases effective stress, potentially causing opposite movements. Base rebound and neighbouring settlement can occur together, so one level or displacement cannot represent the site. Retain layer compressibility and drainage time scales in the assessment.§effectiveStressIncrease=gammaW*drawdown=9.81 kN/m3*4 m=39.24 kPa§同步分析坑底回彈、鄰地沉陷與分層孔隙水壓~Analyze base rebound, neighbouring settlement and interval pore pressures together§只觀察坑內回彈漏掉外部壓密，鄰房逐步差異沉陷~Monitoring only internal rebound misses external consolidation and differential building settlement§坑底回彈就代表周邊地層不可能同時沉陷~Base rebound means surrounding ground cannot simultaneously settle
分階段監測與模型校核~Staged monitoring and model checks§逆打結構每增加樓板或移除土體，邊界都會改變，監測資料必須依工序分段解讀。將所有讀值擬合成一條連續曲線會混淆剛度改變與地層變化；應比較每個階段增量和預測區間，而非只檢查最終最大位移。~Every added slab or removed soil layer changes the boundary, requiring stage-based interpretation. Fitting all readings with one smooth curve confuses stiffness changes with ground behaviour. Compare stage increments with prediction ranges rather than checking only the final maximum movement.§stageIncrement=wallMoveAfter-wallMoveBefore=18 mm-11 mm=7 mm§把每階段牆移增量與板柱應變及實際工序共同對照~Compare stage wall increments with slab-column strain and actual sequence§中間階段異常被最終回復掩蓋，漏掉已發生的接頭損傷~An intermediate anomaly is hidden by later recovery despite existing joint damage§最終位移符合就表示所有中間施工階段都正常~A compliant final displacement proves every intermediate construction stage was normal
基礎接手與永久抗浮~Foundation transfer and permanent uplift§底板完成後，預置柱、永久柱、樁和連續壁的荷載分配可能改變，還需承受地下水恢復。施工支承不會自動消失，接頭和剛度決定轉移比例；抗浮評估應避免把同一根樁的承壓和拉拔能力同時當作可任意動員。~Base completion changes load sharing among plunge columns, permanent columns, piles and walls while groundwater recovers. Temporary support does not disappear automatically; joint and stiffness govern transfer. Uplift assessment must not treat a pile's compression and tension capacities as freely simultaneous resources.§hydrostaticUplift=9.81 kN/m3*12 m*100 m2=11772 kN§檢查底板接頭、樁荷重與恢復水位時的結構反應~Check base joints, pile loads and structural response as groundwater recovers§永久抗浮未含水位恢復，底板上抬並拉裂牆板接面~Omitted groundwater recovery lifts the base and cracks its wall interfaces§施工期持續抽水就能永久免除抗浮設計~Continuous construction dewatering permanently removes the need for uplift design
施工歷程與永久文件~Construction history and permanent records§逆打交接需要保留曾經發生的荷載與變形，而不只是最後幾何。埋入柱、接頭和臨時開口關閉後不易追查，若缺少版本，未來改造可能破壞仍在工作的傳力路徑；永久管理應知道哪些構件兼具歷史施工角色。~Handover needs historical loads and movements as well as final geometry. Embedded columns, joints and closed temporary openings become difficult to investigate. Missing revisions can let later alterations interrupt an active load path, so management must understand members with both construction and permanent roles.§recordLinkage=stagesWithVerifiedRecords/requiredStages=11/12=91.7 percent§按構件編號連結工序、荷載、接頭檢查與竣工版本~Link sequence, loads, joint inspections and as-built revisions by component identifier§改造人員誤拆看似臨時構件，破壞永久樓板支撐~Renovation removes an apparently temporary member and disrupts permanent slab support§工程完工後所有施工階段資料都沒有維護價值~Construction-stage records have no maintenance value after project completion
''')
add('b168','整合沉管預製質量、浮力、穩性與海事介面~Integrate immersed-tube fabrication mass, buoyancy, stability and marine interfaces','浮力平衡不代表穩性或可操作性，拖航與沉放需專業海事計畫。~Buoyancy balance does not establish stability or operability; towing and immersion require specialist marine plans.','結構質量由 60000 增為 63000 t，海水密度 1.025 t/m3，平衡排水體積由 58536.6 增為 61463.4 m3；質量增加 5% 不代表穩性也改善 5%。~Mass rising from 60000 to 63000 t at seawater density 1.025 t/m3 increases displacement from 58536.6 to 61463.4 m3; five percent more mass does not imply five percent better stability.',r'''
預製體積與結構質量~Fabrication volume and structural mass§浮運計算需要所有混凝土、鋼材、設備和臨時構件的質量，不能只採名義混凝土體積。公噸是質量而非力，受力計算還需重力加速度；材料密度與實際幾何誤差應分開追蹤，才可判斷預測吃水差異來源。~Flotation needs the mass of concrete, steel, equipment and temporary works, not nominal concrete volume alone. Tonnes measure mass rather than force; force calculations also require gravity. Track density and geometry errors separately to diagnose differences between predicted and observed draft.§structuralMass=volume*density=25000 m3*2.4 t/m3=60000 t§把分段體積、材料密度與設備增減連結到質量帳~Link segment volumes, densities and equipment changes to the mass ledger§臨時設備未入帳讓實際吃水增加，預計乾舷餘裕消失~Unrecorded temporary equipment increases draft and consumes expected freeboard§管節混凝土圖說體積就能代表全部浮運質量~Drawing concrete volume alone represents the entire flotation mass
排水體積與浮力平衡~Displacement and buoyancy balance§靜浮時浮力等於總重量，所需排水體積由總質量除水密度得到。海水密度隨鹽度和溫度變化，內部進水還會同時改變質量與自由液面；平衡只說明垂直合力，不保證遇擾動後會回復原姿態。~At static flotation buoyancy balances total weight, giving displacement as mass divided by water density. Salinity and temperature change density, while internal flooding changes mass and free surfaces. Vertical balance alone does not establish restoration after a disturbance or a safe marine operation.§displacement=mass/rho=60000 t/(1.025 t/m3)=58536.6 m3§將實測水密度、吃水及質量帳共同檢核浮力平衡~Check measured water density and draft against the mass ledger§沿用錯誤水密度造成吃水預測偏差，局部淨距不足~Incorrect water density biases draft prediction and leaves insufficient local clearance§能漂浮就代表管節遇到傾斜一定能自行恢復~A floating element necessarily returns upright after any inclination
重心與初始橫向穩性~Centre of gravity and initial transverse stability§初始穩性取決於重心、浮心與水線面幾何，不只是總浮力。小角度穩心高只描述平衡附近斜率，大角度扶正力臂仍需獨立分析；臨時設備放高或壓載分布不當，可能在總重量不變時明顯改變穩性。~Initial stability depends on gravity centre, buoyancy centre and waterplane geometry rather than total buoyancy alone. Small-angle metacentric height describes the local restoring slope; large-angle arms require separate analysis. High equipment or altered ballast can change stability without changing total mass.§GM=KB+BM-KG=3.0 m+8.0 m-9.5 m=1.5 m before free-surface correction§核對設備與壓載重心，對照專業穩性模型及傾斜證據~Check equipment and ballast centres against specialist stability modelling and inclination evidence§質量不變卻提高重心，初始扶正能力下降~Raising the gravity centre reduces initial restoring ability despite unchanged mass§總重量不變就代表浮體穩性完全不變~Unchanged total mass means flotation stability is completely unchanged
自由液面與穩性折減~Free surfaces and stability reduction§未滿的壓載艙液體會隨傾斜移動，產生減少扶正能力的自由液面效應。其影響取決於液面面積慣性矩而非僅水量，寬而淺的艙可能比窄艙更敏感；隔艙和液位狀態需要在每個浮運階段明確列示。~Liquid in partially filled tanks shifts with heel and reduces restoring action through free-surface effects. The effect depends on liquid-surface second moment rather than volume alone; broad shallow tanks can be especially sensitive. Define compartments and fill state at every flotation stage.§GMcorrection=rhoLiquid*Ifree/mass=1.0 t/m3*6000 m4/60000 t=0.10 m§按實際艙格液位檢查自由液面及修正後穩性~Check free surfaces and corrected stability for the actual compartment levels§只計壓載降低重心卻漏算自由液面，穩性被高估~Crediting ballast for lowering gravity while omitting free surfaces overstates stability§加水壓載一定只會改善而不會降低穩性~Adding water ballast always improves stability and can never reduce it
吃水變化與水線面~Draft change and waterplane area§小幅增重的吃水變化可用新增質量除水密度和水線面積估算，但水線面隨吃水變化時需重新計算。縱向質量位置還會造成俯仰，不應把平均吃水套到每個角落；測量須同時辨認平均下沉和姿態變化。~Small added mass changes mean draft according to density and waterplane area, provided area remains approximately constant. Longitudinal mass position also changes trim, so average draft cannot represent every corner. Distinguish mean immersion from pitch and roll in the survey.§deltaDraft=deltaMass/(rho*Awaterplane)=500 t/(1.025 t/m3*4000 m2)=0.122 m§比較四角吃水、壓載位置及水線面幾何變化~Compare corner drafts, ballast position and changes in waterplane geometry§平均吃水合格卻一端俯仰過深，水下淨距被局部吃掉~Acceptable mean draft hides excessive trim and local loss of underwater clearance§平均吃水值就能代表管節每一端的最低位置~Mean draft represents the lowest position at every end of the element
臨時封艙與水壓合力~Temporary bulkheads and pressure resultant§封艙在浮運期間承受內外水位差，合力與壓力沿高度的分布有關，不能只用底部壓力乘整面積。支承、接頭與滲漏會影響局部受力，還須考慮不同艙室狀態；船體浮力平衡不會自動證明封艙強度。~Bulkheads resist internal-external head differences with a pressure distribution over depth, not bottom pressure uniformly over the area. Supports, joints and leakage affect local response across compartment states. Global flotation balance does not establish bulkhead strength or connection integrity.§F=0.5*gammaWater*b*h^2=0.5*10.055 kN/m3*8 m*(4 m)^2=643.5 kN§將封艙兩側水位、板面變形及接頭滲漏共同記錄~Record water levels on both sides, plate deformation and joint leakage together§以平均吃水忽略局部壓差，封艙接頭承受未檢核反力~Mean draft conceals a local head difference and unchecked bulkhead-joint reactions§浮體整體浮力平衡就足以證明封艙板安全~Global buoyancy balance is sufficient to prove bulkhead safety
預製溫度與節段變形~Fabrication temperature and segment deformation§長大混凝土管節在水化、養護和轉場時經歷溫度變化，支承拘束使自由伸縮轉成應力。短節段的自由變形算例不能直接代表整體接頭力，因為裂縫、徐變與支承摩擦會改變反應；尺寸驗收需註明參考溫度。~Large concrete elements change temperature during hydration, curing and transfer, turning free movement into stress under restraint. A short-segment free-expansion example does not establish joint force because cracking, creep and support friction modify it. State the reference temperature for dimensional acceptance.§freeMovement=alpha*L*dT=1e-5/K*12 m*30 K=0.0036 m=3.6 mm§對照尺寸量測時溫度、支承狀態及裂縫發展~Compare dimensional survey temperature, support state and crack development§不同溫度量得長度被誤判製造超差，引發錯誤接頭調整~Lengths measured at different temperatures appear out of tolerance and prompt the wrong joint adjustment§混凝土管節製造完成後尺寸就永遠不再改變~Concrete element dimensions never change after fabrication is complete
水流阻力與拖航界面~Current drag and tow interface§流體阻力與相對流速平方成正比，流向、投影面積及阻力係數會隨姿態變化。簡式只估準靜態作用，波浪、加速度及拖纜動態另需海事分析；不能把單一阻力數值當成拖具或操作窗口的完整設計。~Drag varies with relative speed squared and changes with orientation, projected area and coefficient. A simple formula estimates quasi-static action only; waves, acceleration and towline dynamics require marine analysis. One drag figure is not a complete towing-system or weather-window design.§Inputs rho=1025 kg/m3, Cd=1.0, A=200 m2, v=1.5 m/s; Fd=0.5*rho*Cd*A*v^2=0.5*1025*1.0*200*(1.5)^2=230625 N=230.6 kN§比較流速方向、管節姿態及拖航系統荷重紀錄~Compare current direction, element attitude and tow-system load records§忽略橫流及動態峰值，平均阻力低卻拖纜瞬間超載~Ignored cross-current and dynamic peaks overload a towline despite modest mean drag§平均水流阻力小就能保證所有拖航動態荷載都小~Low mean current drag guarantees small loads in every towing dynamic event
支承轉換與縱向彎曲~Support transitions and longitudinal bending§管節從預製支座到浮力分布，再到沉放和基床接觸，縱向支承條件多次改變。相同自重在不同分布反力下產生不同彎矩，浮體波浪彎曲也不能用陸上簡支模型替代；每一階段需有自己的荷載及接觸假設。~Support changes from fabrication bearings to distributed buoyancy and then immersion and bedding contact. Equal weight produces different moments under different reactions, and wave bending is not a land-based simple beam. Each stage needs its own loading and contact assumptions with verified transitions.§M=q*L^2/8=100 kN/m*(60 m)^2/8=45000 kNm for an ideal land-based simple span§將支座、浮力分布及基床接觸分別連到管節應變資料~Relate bearing, buoyancy and bedding contact states separately to element strains§借用上一階段支承模型，漏掉轉換時的最大縱向彎矩~Reusing a previous support model misses peak longitudinal bending during transfer§管節自重不變就代表各施工階段彎矩相同~Unchanged self-weight means identical bending moments in every construction stage
浮運放行與資料一致性~Flotation release and record consistency§浮運判斷需要質量、幾何、水密、穩性及設備狀態的共同版本，單項合格不能互相抵消。晚期設備變更可能改變重心和吃水，若未更新計算就使原結論失效；交接應能追溯每項輸入的日期與實際配置。~Release requires consistent versions of mass, geometry, tightness, stability and equipment status; passing one cannot offset failure of another. Late equipment changes alter gravity and draft and can invalidate earlier conclusions. Trace each input to its date and installed configuration rather than a generic certificate.§massDiscrepancy=(verified-estimated)/estimated=(60600-60000) t/60000 t=1 percent§核對最後配置與質量、穩性、水密及幾何文件版本~Audit final configuration against mass, stability, tightness and geometry document revisions§設備改裝未納入海事模型，原放行數據已不對應實體~Equipment changes omitted from the marine model leave release data inconsistent with the element§所有單項曾經合格就代表任何新配置都可放行~Previously passing components authorize release of every later configuration
''')

add('b169','以海床幾何、接觸壓力與沉陷驗證沉管基床~Verify immersed-tunnel bedding through seabed geometry, contact pressure and settlement','測得平整不代表全部接觸，基床與深部地層的長期變形須分開。~Measured levelness does not prove full contact; bedding and deeper-ground deformation require separate assessment.','其餘條件不變，壓縮係數由 0.0002 增為 0.0003 /kPa，簡化沉陷由 50 增為 75 mm；相鄰管節差異仍須轉成接頭轉角檢核。~With other inputs fixed, compressibility rising from 0.0002 to 0.0003 per kPa increases simplified settlement from 50 to 75 mm; differences between elements still require joint-rotation assessment.',r'''
溝槽斷面與開挖體積~Trench section and dredging volume§海床溝槽需容納管節、基床及回填保護，疏浚體積還受邊坡和原地形影響。矩形體積只是物料帳基準，超挖與回淤會改變後續接觸；應將設計斷面與不同時間海床測量配準，不能只用船舶出土量驗收幾何。~The trench accommodates element, bedding and protective fill, with slopes and terrain changing dredged volume. A rectangular estimate is only a material baseline; over-dredging and resedimentation alter contact. Register design and time-stamped seabed surveys rather than accepting geometry from vessel spoil volume alone.§V=width*depth*length=40 m*1 m*200 m=8000 m3 for an assumed rectangular layer§以多期測深斷面比較設計底標高、邊坡及回淤~Compare repeated bathymetry with design base level, slopes and resedimentation§疏浚完成後回淤未重測，管節落在軟泥而非設計基床~Unsurveyed resedimentation leaves the element on soft mud rather than the designed bed§出土量達到設計值就能保證溝槽形狀正確~Design dredged volume guarantees the correct trench shape
淨重與基床平均壓力~Submerged weight and mean bed pressure§基床承受的是管節與回填在水下的有效作用，不能把空氣中自重直接當成同一接觸荷載。浮力、壓載及外部水壓需採一致自由體，若重複扣浮力會低估荷載；平均壓力仍需另查接觸面是否完整。~Bedding carries submerged actions from the element and fill, not simply air weight. Use one consistent free body for buoyancy, ballast and external pressure; subtracting buoyancy twice understates demand. Mean pressure also requires separate confirmation of the actual contact area.§q=netDownwardForce/contactArea=20000 kN/4000 m2=5 kPa§對照壓載及水位狀態，核對所用淨重與接觸面積~Check net force and contact area against ballast and water-level states§重複扣除浮力導致平均壓力偏低，沉陷預測失準~Double-counted buoyancy lowers estimated pressure and mispredicts settlement§空氣中重量與水下基床接觸荷載永遠相同~Air weight always equals the contact load on submerged bedding
深部壓縮與總沉陷~Deep compression and total settlement§平整基床下面的軟弱層仍會壓縮，管節表面施工容差不能代表長期位置穩定。簡化一維沉陷模型使用應力增量、壓縮性和層厚，需區分有效應力和總應力；排水時間與應力歷史會改變實際反應。~Weak layers beneath level bedding can compress, so construction tolerance does not establish long-term position. A one-dimensional settlement model uses stress increment, compressibility and thickness, requiring effective rather than indiscriminate total stress. Drainage time and stress history modify actual response.§s=mv*dSigma*H=0.0002 /kPa*50 kPa*5 m=0.05 m=50 mm§將分層地質壓縮試驗與管節水準、孔隙水壓共同比較~Compare layer compression tests with element levels and pore pressure§只驗收基床表面平整而漏掉深部軟層，長期整體沉降~Surface-level acceptance misses a deep soft layer and long-term settlement follows§基床表面平整就能證明深部地層不會壓縮~A level bed surface proves deeper ground cannot compress
差異沉陷與接頭轉角~Differential settlement and joint rotation§相鄰管節沉陷不同會使接頭旋轉，平均總沉陷小也可能有較大局部角差。單一管節的端點差除長度是弦傾角；本算例額外假定該管節為剛體且相鄰管節保持水平，才可把弦傾角當接頭相對轉角。一般情況須取接頭兩側斜率差，實際還有彎曲及接頭剪力；應沿縱向保留多點量測而不只記兩岸高程。~Different settlement of adjacent elements rotates joints, even when mean settlement is small. Endpoint difference divided by element length is chord inclination. Only the additional assumptions of a rigid element and a horizontal neighboring element make it relative joint rotation here; otherwise compare slopes on both sides. Bending and joint shear also occur. Preserve multiple longitudinal observations rather than relying on the shore-end elevations alone.§chordInclination=settlementDifference/length=20 mm/200000 mm=0.0001 rad; relativeJointRotation=chordInclination only for this rigid element beside an assumed horizontal neighbor§逐管節比較端部高程、縱向曲率與接頭位移~Compare end levels, longitudinal curvature and joint movement for every element§局部軟區造成端部轉角，密封位移需求被平均沉陷漏判~A soft local zone rotates an end and mean settlement misses the seal demand§總平均沉陷很小就代表接頭不會轉動~Small overall average settlement means joints cannot rotate
墊層厚度與材料收支~Bedding thickness and material balance§基床材料厚度需配合原海床起伏，理論鋪料體積不能證明每一位置都達到厚度。水下離析和流失會改變局部級配，鬆鋪與壓實體積也不同；收支帳應與測深和材料性質一起解讀，而非用總噸數取代幾何驗證。~Bedding thickness follows underlying terrain, and theoretical placement volume does not prove every point. Underwater segregation and loss change grading, while loose and compacted volumes differ. Interpret mass balance with bathymetry and material properties rather than replacing geometry with total tonnage.§Vbed=area*thickness=4000 m2*0.60 m=2400 m3§比較鋪料前後海床面、材料密度及可追溯批次~Compare pre/post-placement surfaces, material density and traceable batches§局部薄層被其他區域超填平均掉，形成不均勻支承~Local thin bedding is averaged against overfill elsewhere and creates uneven support§材料總量足夠就能保證每處基床厚度相同~Adequate total material guarantees equal bedding thickness everywhere
粒徑分布與水下離析~Grading and underwater segregation§粒徑級配影響可整平性、滲透和抗流失能力，但均勻係數只是分布的一個指標。水下放料可能使細料和粗料分離，取樣若只來自岸上料堆便無法反映原位狀態；材料相容要與基底土層和水流一起評估。~Grading influences leveling, permeability and resistance to loss, but uniformity coefficient describes only one distribution feature. Underwater placement can separate fines and coarse grains, so shore-stockpile samples may not represent installed bedding. Assess compatibility with underlying soil and currents together.§Cu=d60/d10=4.0 mm/0.5 mm=8, not a complete filter criterion§比較料源與水下代表樣本的完整粒徑曲線~Compare full grading curves from the source and representative submerged samples§細料被流走形成粗骨架，局部孔隙與接觸剛度改變~Washed-out fines leave a coarse skeleton with changed voids and contact stiffness§均勻係數相同就代表兩種基床材料性能完全相同~Equal uniformity coefficients prove identical performance of two bedding materials
高點接觸與局部壓力~High-point contact and local pressure§少數高點可能先接觸管節，使荷載集中而其他區域仍懸空。總平均壓力因此會低估局部壓碎或管底彎曲，接觸面隨沉放及材料變形逐步改變；應區分設計底面積與已證實的受壓面積。~A few high spots engage first and concentrate load while other areas remain unsupported. Mean pressure then understates crushing or underside bending, and contact evolves during settlement and material deformation. Distinguish design base area from verified loaded area rather than assuming full bearing.§localPressure=20000 kN/200 m2=100 kPa versus 5 kPa over 4000 m2§將高程殘差、接觸證據與管底應變共同比對~Compare elevation residuals, contact evidence and element-bottom strain§基床高點局部壓碎造成突然坐落與接頭姿態變化~High spots crush locally and cause abrupt seating and changed joint alignment§平均基床壓力低就能保證局部不會壓碎~Low mean bedding pressure guarantees no local crushing
測深誤差與共同基準~Bathymetric uncertainty and shared datum§水下測量受水位、聲速、姿態與定位誤差影響，單一漂亮網格不代表垂直精度。獨立隨機分量可平方和合成，但共同基準偏差不能這樣消除；需保存原始校正及不同測期使用的垂直基準，避免將儀器差當成基床變化。~Bathymetry depends on water level, sound speed, attitude and position, not just a smooth grid. Independent random terms combine by root-sum-square, while shared datum bias does not disappear that way. Preserve calibration and vertical references across epochs to distinguish instrument differences from bed changes.§Inputs independent component standard uncertainties=0.02,0.03,0.02 m; sigmaCombined=sqrt(0.02^2+0.03^2+0.02^2)=0.0412 m for independent random components§核對水位基準、聲速剖面及交叉測線閉合差~Check water-level datum, sound-speed profiles and cross-line closure residuals§兩期水位基準不一致造成假高點，導致錯誤整平判讀~Inconsistent epoch datums create false high spots and misdirect leveling assessment§把所有誤差平方和開根號就能消除共同基準偏差~Root-sum-square of errors eliminates every shared datum bias
沖刷與長期基床保護~Scour and long-term bed protection§水流可能移動保護層或細粒，使原本接觸良好的基床逐漸失去支承。局部流速受地形、船舶和構造邊緣影響，不等於遠處平均流速；保護設計與監測需確認材料穩定、濾層連續和可觀察的海床變化。~Currents can move cover or fines and progressively remove bedding support. Local speed reflects topography, vessels and structural edges rather than distant mean flow. Protection and monitoring need evidence of material stability, filter continuity and observable seabed change instead of a single current reading.§velocityPressure=0.5*rho*v^2=0.5*1025 kg/m3*(2 m/s)^2=2050 Pa§以重複測深、局部流速及保護層完整性共同追蹤~Track repeated bathymetry, local currents and protection-layer continuity together§邊緣細料流失形成空洞，管節初始驗收合格仍逐年變形~Edge-fine loss creates voids and gradual movement despite initial acceptance§管節落位驗收後基床支承就永遠不會改變~Bedding support never changes after placement acceptance
基床交接與長期基線~Bedding handover and long-term baseline§水下基床完工後不可直接目視，其數位地形與取樣資料是後續診斷的基準。驗收圖應區分實測、插值及未覆蓋區，還要連到測量時間和水位；把整張彩色圖都當作同精度證據會隱藏關鍵盲區。~After placement, bedding is no longer directly visible, making digital terrain and sample records diagnostic baselines. Distinguish measured, interpolated and uncovered zones and link time and water level. Treating a coloured map as uniformly accurate conceals critical evidence gaps for later maintenance.§surveyCoverage=measuredArea/requiredArea=3800 m2/4000 m2=95 percent§將測線覆蓋、誤差、取樣及管節位置索引到同一座標~Index survey coverage, uncertainty, samples and element position to common coordinates§未測區被平滑插值掩蓋，日後沉陷缺少可追溯基準~Smoothing hides an unsurveyed zone and later settlement lacks a traceable baseline§地形圖看起來連續就代表每一點都實際量測過~A continuous-looking terrain map proves every point was directly measured
''')

add('b170','沉管接頭幾何、壓縮接觸與雙重水密屏障~Immersed-joint geometry, compression contact and dual sealing barriers','接頭算例將剛體位移與橡膠變形分開；實際密封反力需特定斷面、溫度、老化及試驗資料。~Joint examples separate rigid-body movement from rubber deformation; actual seal reactions require profile, temperature, aging and test data.','角差從 0.0005 增至 0.0008 rad，使 30 m 寬面上的幾何差由 15 增至 24 mm，增加六成；反力不一定同比。~Increasing angular mismatch from 0.0005 to 0.0008 rad raises the differential across a 30 m face from 15 to 24 mm, a sixty-percent increase; reaction need not scale proportionally.',r'''
端面姿態與初始接觸~End-face attitude and initial contact§接頭兩端面並非只需中心對準，偏航、俯仰和翹曲會使密封圈局部先接觸。第一接觸點承受的壓縮可能遠大於平均值，因而幾何差應沿整個周邊呈現；剛體角差模型只識別不均勻性，不能給出橡膠反力分布。~Coincident centers do not ensure matching end faces: yaw, pitch and warping create early local seal contact. The first contact can compress far more than the average, so map mismatch around the perimeter. A rigid-angle model identifies nonuniformity but cannot determine rubber reaction distribution.§differential=width*angle=30 m*0.0005 rad=0.015 m=15 mm§比較兩端面共同座標的周邊點雲與接觸順序~Compare perimeter point clouds in common coordinates with the sequence of contact§中心線合格但端面角差使密封一側過壓而另一側未接觸~Acceptable centerline alignment conceals excessive compression on one seal side and a gap on the other§兩管節中心對準就代表周邊密封必定均勻接觸~Aligned element centers guarantee uniform contact around the entire seal
主密封壓縮與反力曲線~Primary-seal compression and reaction curves§Gina 類主密封利用端面壓縮建立接觸，但空心斷面與材料非線性使反力不會簡單正比壓縮率。製造商試驗曲線應對應實際斷面和溫度，接縫、轉角及長期鬆弛另行評估；幾何壓縮率只能作版本與尺寸核對。~A Gina-type primary seal develops contact through end compression, but hollow geometry and nonlinear rubber prevent reaction from scaling directly with compression ratio. Match manufacturer tests to the profile and temperature and assess corners, splices and relaxation separately. A geometric ratio checks dimensions and configuration only.§compressionRatio=closure/profileHeight=40 mm/100 mm=0.40§將周邊壓縮量與相符斷面試驗曲線及材料批次比對~Compare perimeter compression with matching profile tests and material batches§借用不同斷面曲線高估接觸反力，局部水壓超過有效密封能力~Using another profile curve overstates contact reaction and leaves local water pressure beyond effective sealing capacity§橡膠壓縮率相同就代表任何密封斷面的反力相同~Equal rubber compression ratios imply equal reaction for every seal profile
壓差合攏與受力邊界~Pressure-assisted closure and load boundaries§接合階段內外壓差對封閉投影面產生軸向合力，經管節、接頭與支承形成平衡。計算面積應是壓差實際作用的有效面，不能混用水下面積或密封橡膠面積；摩擦、姿態和臨時構造使實際位移不能只由壓力推得。~During joining, pressure difference over a closed projected area produces axial force balanced through the element, joint and supports. Use the actual pressure-boundary area rather than submerged surface or rubber contact area. Friction, attitude and temporary works prevent pressure alone from predicting displacement.§axialResultant=dp*effectiveArea=0.20 MPa*100 m2=20 MN§對照壓力分區圖、端面位移與接頭受力路徑~Compare pressure-zone diagrams, end-face displacement and joint load paths§漏列與外水連通的腔室，錯算有效壓差及合攏力~An omitted chamber connected to external water produces the wrong pressure difference and closure force§外水壓乘全部濕表面就等於接頭軸向合攏力~External pressure times every wet surface equals the axial joint-closing force
次級密封與膜面荷載~Secondary seals and membrane loading§Omega 類次級密封容許接頭相對位移，並提供與主密封不同的水密屏障。壓力乘跨距是每單位長度的橫向合力，不是膜張力；張力還取決於鼓出幾何、邊界固定和材料變形，夾具與角部不能從均勻薄膜模型略去。~An Omega-type secondary seal accommodates relative movement and forms a barrier distinct from the primary seal. Pressure times span gives transverse resultant per unit length, not membrane tension. Tension also depends on bulging geometry, restraints and material deformation; clamps and corners require separate assessment.§transverseResultantPerLength=p*span=0.20 MPa*0.30 m=60 kN/m; this is not membrane tension§把次級膜鼓出形狀、夾具位移與壓差試驗結果連結~Relate secondary-membrane bulge, clamp movement and differential-pressure tests§把橫向合力誤當膜張力，漏估夾持區剝離與角部應變~Treating transverse resultant as tension misses clamp peeling and corner strain§壓力乘密封跨距即可直接得到所有位置的膜張力~Pressure times seal span directly gives membrane tension at every location
溫度伸縮與軸向位移~Thermal expansion and axial movement§管節溫度改變可能透過接頭釋放位移，也可能因基床摩擦和相鄰約束累積軸力。自由伸縮是假想無拘束上限情境之一，不能同時又假定全拘束應力；維護判讀須對應量測溫度與實際滑移邊界，分開季節變化和永久漂移。~Element temperature changes can release movement at joints or accumulate force through bedding friction and neighboring restraints. Free expansion is a hypothetical unrestrained case and cannot simultaneously imply full-restraint stress. Relate monitoring temperature to slip boundaries to separate seasonal changes from permanent drift.§freeExpansion=alpha*L*dT=1e-5/K*200 m*15 K=0.030 m§比較管節溫度、接頭軸向開度及長期位置趨勢~Compare element temperature, axial joint opening and long-term position trends§季節開度被誤判永久沉陷，或永久漂移被季節平均掩蓋~Seasonal opening is mistaken for settlement or averaging conceals permanent drift§長管節的自由熱伸縮必定全部集中在單一接頭~All free thermal expansion of a long element concentrates at one joint
差異沉陷與接頭轉角~Differential settlement and joint rotation§相鄰基床沉陷差使接頭發生轉角和剪位移，密封上緣與下緣的開度因而不同。本算例假定一管節為剛體且相鄰管節維持水平，因此單段弦傾角等於接頭相對轉角；若兩側都轉動，應改用兩側斜率差。管節本身彎曲及接頭剪力鍵約束也會重新分配變形；必須同時觀察接頭和管節的長基線高程。~Differential bedding settlement rotates and shears a joint, producing different openings at its top and bottom. This example assumes one rigid element beside a horizontal neighbor, so its chord inclination equals relative joint rotation. If both sides rotate, use their slope difference instead. Element bending and shear-key restraints also redistribute movement. Monitor both the joint and long-baseline element elevations to distinguish these contributions.§relativeJointRotation=0.020 m/200 m=0.00010 rad only for a rigid element beside a horizontal neighbor; openingDifference=relativeJointRotation*10 m=0.001 m§比較長基線沉陷、接頭四角開度與剪位移~Compare long-baseline settlement, four-corner opening and joint shear movement§單點開度正常卻四角變化不一致，漏掉轉角造成的局部卸壓~One normal opening measurement conceals corner differences and rotation-induced local unloading§量測接頭中央一個開度就能代表整圈密封變形~One central opening measurement represents deformation around the entire seal
剪力鍵承壓與接觸偏心~Shear-key bearing and eccentric contact§剪力鍵限制管節相對橫移並將剪力傳給混凝土，接觸位置取決於間隙、裝配與差異沉陷。平均承壓只適用已知有效面積，邊緣接觸會伴隨劈裂和局部彎曲；不能把整塊外觀面積直接當作同時承壓面。~Shear keys restrain relative transverse movement and transmit shear into concrete, with contact governed by gaps, assembly and settlement. Average bearing requires a known effective area; edge contact introduces splitting and local bending. The whole visible face is not automatically active bearing area.§meanBearing=shear/effectiveArea=1000 kN/0.50 m2=2000 kPa=2 MPa§核對剪力鍵間隙、接觸痕跡與鄰近混凝土裂縫~Check shear-key gaps, contact marks and nearby concrete cracks§鍵角先接觸引發混凝土劈裂，平均承壓計算仍顯示偏低~Corner-first contact splits concrete while an average bearing calculation remains low§剪力鍵外觀面積全部都會同時均勻承受剪力~The full visible shear-key area always carries shear uniformly
分區滲漏與來源辨識~Compartment leakage and source diagnosis§接頭集水量可能來自主密封、次級密封、螺栓穿孔或周邊施工縫，不是單憑出水位置就能定位缺口。比較分區壓力與時間響應可縮小來源，總流量還受外水位影響；低流量不能證明兩重屏障均保持完整。~Collected joint water can originate at primary seals, secondary seals, penetrations or adjacent construction joints. Outlet location alone does not locate the breach. Compartment pressure and time response narrow the source, while external water level affects total flow; low flow does not demonstrate two intact barriers.§collectedFlow=12 L/30 min=0.40 L/min§同步記錄分區水壓、集水量及外水位變化~Record compartment pressure, collected flow and external water-level changes together§匯集管混接使異處滲水被歸因接頭，修繕後流量不降~Combined collection lines misattribute remote seepage to a joint and repairs do not reduce flow§接頭集水少就能證明主次兩道密封都毫無缺陷~Low collected joint flow proves both primary and secondary seals are defect-free
應力鬆弛與長期密封~Stress relaxation and long-term sealing§橡膠在近固定壓縮下仍會應力鬆弛，溫度、老化和化學環境共同改變長期接觸反力。短期保持率只是特定試驗條件的比較，不是現場壽命或剩餘承壓能力；長期評估需保持幾何變形與材料劣化資料之間的對應。~Rubber relaxes under nearly fixed compression, with temperature, aging and chemistry altering long-term contact force. Short-term retention compares specified test conditions, not field lifetime or remaining pressure capacity. Long-term assessment must link material degradation evidence with actual geometric deformation histories.§forceRetention=180 kN/240 kN=0.75=75 percent at equal imposed compression§比較相同壓縮與溫度的保載試驗及接頭歷時位移~Compare sustained-compression tests at equal temperature with joint movement histories§將加速試驗小時數直接當服役年數，錯估長期密封反力~Equating accelerated-test hours directly to service years misestimates long-term seal reaction§壓縮量固定就表示橡膠密封反力永遠不會降低~Fixed compression means rubber sealing reaction never decreases over time
屏障獨立性與交接檔案~Barrier independence and handover records§主次密封若共用同一失效夾持件或受同一大位移破壞，就不構成完全獨立的備援。交接需對應各屏障試驗、幾何、材料和可檢查部位，完整率僅顯示證據缺口；缺失一項關鍵試驗不能由更多非關鍵紀錄補足。~Primary and secondary seals are not fully independent if they share a failed restraint or suffer the same excessive movement. Handover links separate barrier tests, geometry, materials and accessible locations. Record completeness reveals evidence gaps; many minor records cannot compensate for a missing critical barrier test.§traceableTests=18/20=90 percent; completeness is not reliability§逐項對照兩道屏障試驗與共同失效構件清單~Reconcile individual barrier tests with the inventory of shared failure components§雙重密封共用的夾具失效，同時破壞被誤認為獨立的備援~A shared clamp failure defeats two barriers incorrectly treated as independent redundancy§只要安裝兩道密封就必定得到完全獨立的雙重保障~Installing two seals always creates completely independent redundant protection
''')
